\section*{Question 6}

\begin{tabular}[t]{|l|l|l|l|l|}
\hline \(x\) & \(f(x)\) & \(f^{\prime}(x)\) & \(g(x)\) & \(g^{\prime}(x)\) \\
\hline 1 & -6 & 3 & 2 & 8 \\
\hline 2 & 2 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\
\hline 3 & 8 & 7 & 6 & 2 \\
\hline 6 & 4 & 5 & 3 & -1 \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
The functions \(f\) and \(g\) have continuous second derivatives. The table above gives values of the functions and their derivatives at selected values of \(x\).
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] Let \(k(x)=f(g(x))\). Write an equation for the line tangent to the graph of \(k\) at \(x=3\).
\item[(b)] Let \(h(x)=\frac{g(x)}{f(x)}\). Find \(h^{\prime}(1)\).
\item[(c)] Evaluate \(\int_{1}^{3} f^{\prime \prime}(2 x) d x\).
\item[(a)]
\[
\begin{aligned}
& k(3)=f(g(3))=f(6)=4 \\
& k^{\prime}(3)=f^{\prime}(g(3)) \cdot g^{\prime}(3)=f^{\prime}(6) \cdot 2=5 \cdot 2=10
\end{aligned}
\]
An equation for the tangent line is \(y=10(x-3)+4\).
\item[(b)]
\[
\begin{aligned}
h^{\prime}(1) & =\frac{f(1) \cdot g^{\prime}(1)-g(1) \cdot f^{\prime}(1)}{(f(1))^{2}} \\
& =\frac{(-6) \cdot 8-2 \cdot 3}{(-6)^{2}}=\frac{-54}{36}=-\frac{3}{2}
\end{aligned}
\]
\item[(c)]
\[
\begin{aligned}
\int_{1}^{3} f^{\prime \prime}(2 x) d x & =\frac{1}{2}\left[f^{\prime}(2 x)\right]_{1}^{3}=\frac{1}{2}\left[f^{\prime}(6)-f^{\prime}(2)\right] \\
& =\frac{1}{2}[5-(-2)]=\frac{7}{2}
\end{aligned}
\]
\end{itemize}
\(3:\left\{\begin{array}{l}2: \text { slope at } x=3 \\ 1: \text { equation for tangent line }\end{array}\right.\)
\(3:\left\{\begin{array}{l}2: \text { expression for } h^{\prime}(1) \\ 1: \text { answer }\end{array}\right.\)
\(3:\left\{\begin{array}{l}2: \text { antiderivative } \\ 1: \text { answer }\end{array}\right.\)
